<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan to tender for 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to tender for 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association will tender on Friday for two shipments totalling 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The shipments contain Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW) and White Wheat (WW) and are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p>Shipment Type  Tonnes  Delivery Date</p>
<p>  One			 Oct 20- Nov 10</p>
<p>	    DNS   17,400</p>
<p>	    HRW    7,100</p>
<p>	     WW    9,500</p>
<p>  Two			 Nov 5-25</p>
<p>	    DNS   16,100</p>
<p>	    HRW    9,900</p>
<p>Major Taiwan wheat buying companies in the association include President Enterprise, Tai Yu Products, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Lien Hwa Industry and other wheat millers.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
